  clock: 3  # b230
  nonce: b230  # b230
  message: "Fixed in PR (dev 261c7921d2).\n\nBehavioral evidence, analyze_cpp on merged dev, the item's pimpl shape:\n  class Impl { int Generate(int,int); };\n  class Tts { int Generate(int,int) const; std::unique_ptr<Impl> impl_; };\n  int Tts::Generate(int a, int b) const { return impl_->Generate(a, b); }\n  -> Tts::Generate -> Impl::Generate.\n  It was Tts::Generate -> Tts::Generate, a false self-call.\nProduction-path tests: test_cpp_explicit_receiver.py. They cover a field (unique_ptr / raw pointer), a local, parameters by pointer and by reference, a wrapped declarator, an inline member, and an inherited member (receiver_type_hint), plus three controls:\n- an untyped `auto` receiver: not bound, no enclosing_class stamp;\n- implicit and explicit `this`: still bind their own class;\n- a smart pointer's own `.reset()`: not the pointee's.\n\nFix: an explicit receiver other than `this` is typed from its declaration: a local or parameter first, else a field of the caller's class via class_field_types.\n- A typed call binds T::m.\n- For a project class T that does not declare m, the call gets an unresolved edge with receiver_type_hint=T.\n- An untyped receiver never takes the enclosing class as its path hint, a same-file short-name hit, or an enclosing_class stamp.\n\nCorpus, call sites where src == dst, vs dev:\n  sherpa-onnx 994 -> 41\n  grpc 1,531 -> 336\n  whisper.cpp 328 -> 147\n  modsecurity 101 -> 15\nMost lost resolved edges were RETARGETED: sherpa 2,073 of 2,194, and 12 of 12 sampled were correct (s->NumFramesReady -> OnlineStream, model_->Run -> OfflineTtsVitsModel::Run).\nUntyped receivers (auto locals, range-for variables) gave up their short-name binds: grpc 6,570, sherpa 121.\n\nRemaining: 10 explicit-receiver self-calls on sherpa-onnx come from methods of a class declared with a qualified name (`class OnlineStream::Impl { ... }`). Those methods are registered with bare names, so the receiver has no owner to type through. Filed separately."  # b230
